      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area first drew settlers in the 1770s, when pioneers like William Reed cleared land at Young Woman's Creek before formal land titles existed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/north_bend_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "North Bend’s earliest European settlement is the oldest in Chapman Township, dating back to the 1770s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/north_bend_pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A short-lived railroad, the North Bend and Kettle Creek Railroad, ran through the town from 1889 until about 1903, hauling timber from nearby forests.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/north_bend_pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community sits at roughly 673 feet above sea level, placing it in a valley that moderates its humid continental climate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
